    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 47)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, international espionage, and FBI docudrama radio history (1943–1970):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 47)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Inspector_West_1970_08_24_C.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Murder Wears Veil 5</code>, <code>Inspector West BBC 1970</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Murder Wears a Veil (Part 5 — Patrick Barr as Inspector West — BBC)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1970-08-24<br>7:30 PM BST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>BBC Radio Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Patrick Barr</strong> (Inspector West), <strong>Avril Angers</strong>, <strong>John Hollis</strong></td>\n<td><strong>John Creasey</strong> (Author), <strong>Cynthia Pughe</strong>, <strong>John Browell</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;British&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Chief Inspector Roger &#39;Handsome&#39; West and Scotland Yard detectives trace the poison-laced veil back to a Mayfair beauty salon, cornering the blackmail syndicate in a midnight London rooftop showdown.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Your_FBI_1945_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>This is Your FBI 1945</code>, <code>Penicillin Hijackers FBI</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Medical Penicillin Hijackers (Stacy Harris as Agent Jim Taylor — Equitable)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blue Net (WJZ)</strong><br>1945-08-24<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Equitable Life</strong><br>Assurance Society USA</td>\n<td><strong>Stacy Harris</strong> (Agent Jim Taylor), <strong>Karl Swenson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Jerry Devine</strong> (Producer/Dir.), <strong>Carl Caruso</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Legal&quot;, &quot;Docudrama&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;This is your FBI, the official broadcast presented with the cooperation of J. Edgar Hoover...&quot; Special Agent Jim Taylor leads a federal task force to break up a wartime black market penicillin hijacking ring diverting life-saving medical supplies from military hospitals.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Your_FBI_1951_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Bad Samaritan</code>, <code>Agent Jim Taylor 1951</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Bad Samaritan (Stacy Harris as Special Agent Jim Taylor — Equitable)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1951-08-24<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Equitable Life</strong><br>Assurance Society USA</td>\n<td><strong>Stacy Harris</strong> (Jim Taylor), <strong>Herb Vigran</strong>, <strong>William Conrad</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Jerry Devine</strong> (Writer/Dir.), <strong>Carl Caruso</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Legal&quot;, &quot;Docudrama&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>FBI Special Agent Jim Taylor pursues a confidence man who poses as a benevolent Good Samaritan offering financial rescue to distraught widows, swindling life insurance benefits before staging staged accidents.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>High_Adventure_1954_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Sun in the West</code>, <code>High Adventure 1954</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Sun in the West (Starring John Dehner &amp; Lawrence Dobkin — High Adventure)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1954-08-24<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Frontier Drama Showcase</td>\n<td><strong>John Dehner</strong>, <strong>Lawrence Dobkin</strong>, <strong>Parley Baer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>George Bamber</strong> (Writer), <strong>William N. Robson</strong>, <strong>Jack McCoy</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>A gritty frontier tale of a rugged fur trapper guide leading an ill-prepared pioneer wagon train through treacherous Mojave desert canyons and hostile territory in a desperate race against starvation.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Beat_Band_1943_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Beat The Band 1943</code>, <code>Hildegarde Ted Weems Kix</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Musical Riddles (Starring Hildegarde &amp; Ted Weems with Perry Como — Kix)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Red (WEAF)</strong><br>1943-08-24<br>10:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>General Mills, Inc.</strong><br>Kix Breakfast Cereal</td>\n<td><strong>Hildegarde</strong>, <strong>Ted Weems Orchestra</strong>, <strong>Perry Como</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arthur Kurlan</strong> (Director), <strong>Tom Reddy</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Quiz&quot;, &quot;Game Show&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Incomparable Hildegarde and bandleader Ted Weems test the musical knowledge of orchestra members with listener-submitted song riddles, featuring velvety crooning from young Perry Como and Elmo Tanner&#39;s whistling solos for Kix Cereal.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Man_Called_X_1951_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Cairo Smuggling Ring</code>, <code>Ken Thurston Agent X</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Cairo Arms Bazaar (Starring Herbert Marshall as Agent X — RCA Victor)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1951-08-24<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>RCA Victor</strong><br>Television &amp; 45 Records</td>\n<td><strong>Herbert Marshall</strong> (Ken Thurston), <strong>Leon Askin</strong> (Pagon)</td>\n<td><strong>Sydney Zelinka</strong> (Writer), <strong>Jack Johnstone</strong>, <strong>Wendell Niles</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Espionage&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Cold War&quot;, &quot;Thriller&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Wherever there is danger, intrigue, and mystery... there you will find The Man Called X!&quot; Secret intelligence operative Ken Thurston and his roguish sidekick Pagon jet into Cairo to infiltrate a black market munitions bazaar supplying weapons to Mediterranean insurgent groups.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 282</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
