    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 40)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, transatlantic shortwave, and radio comedy history (1932–1956):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 40)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Johnny_Dollar_1956_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Kranesburg Matter Part 5</code>, <code>Johnny Dollar Bob Bailey 1956</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Kranesburg Matter (Part 5 — Bob Bailey as Johnny Dollar — CBS)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1956-08-24<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Radio Mystery Serial</td>\n<td><strong>Bob Bailey</strong> (Johnny Dollar), <strong>Virginia Gregg</strong>, <strong>Parley Baer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>John Dawson</strong> (Writer), <strong>Jack Johnstone</strong>, <strong>Roy Rowan</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Noir&quot;, &quot;Insurance&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Freelance insurance investigator Johnny Dollar traps an elusive art smuggler and recovers valuable stolen Old Master paintings after staging an undercover sting operation in the Kranesburg estate boathouse.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>London_Dark_1940_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>London After Dark Live</code>, <code>Murrow Blitz Shortwave 1940</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;London After Dark: Live from the Blitz (Edward R. Murrow — CBS)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1940-08-24<br>6:30 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS News Live Relay</td>\n<td><strong>Edward R. Murrow</strong>, <strong>Eric Sevareid</strong>, <strong>Larry LeSueur</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS News Transatlantic Unit</strong>, <strong>Bob Trout</strong> (Anchor)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Documentary&quot;, &quot;News&quot;, &quot;World War II&quot;, &quot;Journalism&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>A landmark live transatlantic shortwave broadcast capturing the sounds of wartime London during the Blitz, featuring Edward R. Murrow speaking under the footsteps of pedestrians outside St. Martin-in-the-Fields and church bells ringing during the blackout.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Jack_Benny_1932_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Cellar Broadcast Benny</code>, <code>Jack Benny Canada Dry 1932</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Cellar Broadcast (Jack Benny &amp; Mary Livingstone — Canada Dry)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1932-08-24<br>8:00 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Canada Dry Ginger Ale</strong><br>Canada Dry Beverages</td>\n<td><strong>Jack Benny</strong>, <strong>Mary Livingstone</strong>, <strong>George Olsen Orchestra</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Jack Benny &amp; Harry Conn</strong>, <strong>Bertha Brainard</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vaudeville&quot;, &quot;Satire&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Jack Benny trades zany insults with orchestra leader George Olsen, reads hilarious rhyming poems from Mary Livingstone, and performs comedic violin solos for Canada Dry Ginger Ale.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Jack_Benny_1934_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>House of Rawchild</code>, <code>Jack Benny Chevrolet 1934</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The House of Rawchild (Jack Benny Movie Parody — Chevrolet)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Red (WEAF)</strong><br>1934-08-24<br>10:00 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>General Motors</strong><br>Chevrolet Knee-Action</td>\n<td><strong>Jack Benny</strong>, <strong>Mary Livingstone</strong>, <strong>Frank Parker</strong>, <strong>Don Wilson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Jack Benny &amp; Harry Conn</strong>, <strong>Don Bestor Orchestra</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Parody&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vaudeville&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Jack Benny and his troupe present a riotous film parody of George Arliss&#39;s hit movie <em>The House of Rothschild</em> titled &#39;The House of Rawchild&#39;, complete with penny-pinching gags and musical selections from tenor Frank Parker for Chevrolet.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Perry_Mason_1951_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Case Forged Check</code>, <code>John Larkin Tide Perry Mason</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Forged Check (John Larkin as Perry Mason — Tide)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1951-08-24<br>2:15 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Tide Detergent &amp; Camay</td>\n<td><strong>John Larkin</strong> (Perry Mason), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong> (Della)</td>\n<td><strong>Erle Stanley Gardner</strong>, <strong>Arthur Hanna</strong>, <strong>Bob Dixon</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Legal&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Soap Opera&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Attorney Perry Mason and loyal secretary Della Street cross-examine a nervous bank teller whose forged withdrawal slip implicates an innocent probate clerk in an embezzlement scandal.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Perry_Mason_1954_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Ed Beekmans Daughter</code>, <code>Perry Mason Tide 1954</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Disappearance of Ed Beekman&#39;s Daughter (John Larkin as Perry Mason — Tide)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1954-08-24<br>2:15 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Tide &amp; Spic and Span</td>\n<td><strong>John Larkin</strong> (Perry Mason), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong>, <strong>Mandel Kramer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Erle Stanley Gardner</strong>, <strong>Arthur Hanna</strong>, <strong>Bob Dixon</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Legal&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Soap Opera&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Perry Mason investigates the sudden disappearance of Ed Beekman&#39;s estranged daughter, uncovering that her secret marriage certificate holds the key to an contested waterfront estate.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 240</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
