    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 38)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, British BBC Radio 4, and educational science history (1943–1983):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 38)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Minds_Eye_1983_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Mind&#39;s Eye</code>, <code>Earplay Minds Eye 1983</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Mind&#39;s Eye: Auditory Illusions (Warren Burton — NPR Audio Theatre)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NPR / WHA</strong><br>1983-08-24<br>8:00 PM CDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NPR Audio Theatre</td>\n<td><strong>Roger Babb</strong>, <strong>Bobbie Kramer</strong>, <strong>Norman Blumensaadt</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Warren Burton</strong> (Producer/Director), <strong>Bob Arnold</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Experimental&quot;, &quot;Psychological&quot;, &quot;Audio Drama&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>An atmospheric experimental radio drama exploring memory distortion, soundscape illusion, and psychological hallucination as an audio archivist discovers mysterious auditory patterns recorded on magnetic tape.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Grand_Ole_Opry_1957_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Grand Ole Opry 1957</code>, <code>Red Foley Minnie Pearl</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Live from the Ryman: Red Foley &amp; Ernest Tubb (Prince Albert Opry)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WSM)</strong><br>1957-08-24<br>9:30 PM CST</td>\n<td><strong>R.J. Reynolds Co.</strong><br>Prince Albert Tobacco</td>\n<td><strong>Red Foley</strong>, <strong>Ernest Tubb</strong>, <strong>Minnie Pearl</strong>, <strong>Chet Atkins</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Vito Pellettieri</strong> (Director), <strong>Grant Turner</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Country&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Bluegrass&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Broadcasting live from Nashville&#39;s historic Ryman Auditorium, host Red Foley and Ernest Tubb lead the Opry cast in foot-stomping honky-tonk hits, Chet Atkins guitar solos, and Cousin Minnie Pearl&#39;s hilarious Grinder&#39;s Switch gossip for Prince Albert Tobacco.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Mr_Chameleon_1949_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Vacation Murder Case</code>, <code>Mr Chameleon Bayer 1949</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Vacation Murder Case (Starring Karl Swenson as Mr. Chameleon — Bayer Aspirin)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1949-08-24<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sterling Drug, Inc.</strong><br>Bayer Aspirin &amp; Phillips&#39;</td>\n<td><strong>Karl Swenson</strong> (Mr. Chameleon), <strong>Blaine Stoddard</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Frank &amp; Anne Hummert</strong>, <strong>Richard Leonard</strong>, <strong>Howard Claney</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Whodunit&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Disguise&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;I am Mr. Chameleon, the famous detective who uses disguise to track down murderers...&quot; Undercover master of disguise Mr. Chameleon poses as a relaxed vacationing resort painter in the Adirondacks to trap a ruthless blackmailer who pushed an heiress from a lakeside cliff.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Apple_Tree_1974_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Apple Tree</code>, <code>Daphne du Maurier Apple Tree</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Apple Tree (Daphne du Maurier Chiller — Starring Paul Daneman — BBC)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1974-08-24<br>8:30 PM BST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>BBC Saturday-Night Theatre</td>\n<td><strong>Paul Daneman</strong> (Narrator / Widower), <strong>Elizabeth Morgan</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Daphne du Maurier</strong> (Author), <strong>Michael Hardwick</strong>, <strong>Jane Morgan</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Psychological&quot;, &quot;Horror&quot;, &quot;Suspense&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Adaptation&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Daphne du Maurier&#39;s eerie psychological chiller, a newly widowed man begins to experience unsettling paranoia as he notices an old, twisted apple tree in his orchard exhibiting uncanny, resentful characteristics of his deceased wife.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Research_1943_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>How Good A Scientist</code>, <code>Adventures in Research 1943</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;How Good a Scientist Are You? (Dr. Phillips Thomas — Westinghouse)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Westinghouse</strong><br>1943-08-24<br>7:15 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Westinghouse Electric</strong><br>Industrial Manufacturing</td>\n<td><strong>Dr. Phillips Thomas</strong> (Physicist), <strong>Paul Shannon</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Westinghouse Electric &amp; KDKA Education Department</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Science&quot;, &quot;Educational&quot;, &quot;Quiz&quot;, &quot;Docudrama&quot;, &quot;Technology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Westinghouse research physicist Dr. Phillips Thomas challenges listeners with an interactive scientific aptitude quiz, demonstrating fundamental physical principles of electronics, chemistry, and aerodynamics through everyday household observations for Westinghouse.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Research_1948_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Golden Touch</code>, <code>Alchemy of Metals Westinghouse</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Golden Touch: Alchemy &amp; Metallurgy (Dr. Phillips Thomas — Westinghouse)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Westinghouse</strong><br>1948-08-24<br>7:15 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Westinghouse Electric</strong><br>Industrial Innovation</td>\n<td><strong>Dr. Phillips Thomas</strong> (Physicist), <strong>Paul Shannon</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Westinghouse Electric &amp; KDKA Pittsburgh</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Science&quot;, &quot;Educational&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Technology&quot;, &quot;Docudrama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Dr. Phillips Thomas traces the scientific history of metallurgy and modern synthetic chemistry, demonstrating how modern scientific industrial research surpassed the mythical &#39;golden touch&#39; of ancient alchemists by creating durable alloys and plastics for Westinghouse.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 228</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
