    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 36)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, British BBC Radio 4, and jazz ballroom history (1937–1970):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 36)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Cavallaro_1947_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>On The Avenue</code>, <code>Carmen Cavallaro Sheaffer</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;On the Avenue &amp; Warsaw Concerto (Carmen Cavallaro — Sheaffer Pen)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1947-08-24<br>3:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>W.A. Sheaffer Pen Co.</strong><br>Stratowriter &amp; Fineline</td>\n<td><strong>Carmen Cavallaro</strong>, <strong>Bob Allen</strong> (Vocalist)</td>\n<td><strong>Russell M. Seeds Agency</strong>, <strong>Keith McLeod</strong>, <strong>Doug Gourlay</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Piano&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;, &quot;Jazz&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Poet of the Piano Carmen Cavallaro weaves sparkling keyboard arpeggios through lush orchestral arrangements of Irving Berlin&#39;s &#39;On the Avenue&#39;, &#39;Smoke Gets in Your Eyes&#39;, and &#39;Warsaw Concerto&#39; for Sheaffer Pens.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Benny_Goodman_1937_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Camel Caravan 1937</code>, <code>Goodman Palomar Ballroom</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Live from the Palomar Ballroom: Sing, Sing, Sing (Benny Goodman — Camel)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1937-08-24<br>9:30 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>R.J. Reynolds Co.</strong><br>Camel Cigarettes</td>\n<td><strong>Benny Goodman</strong>, <strong>Harry James</strong>, <strong>Gene Krupa</strong>, <strong>Teddy Wilson</strong>, <strong>Lionel Hampton</strong></td>\n<td><strong>William Esty &amp; Co.</strong>, <strong>Frank Gallop</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Jazz&quot;, &quot;Swing&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;, &quot;Clarinet&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Broadcasting live from the Palomar Ballroom in Los Angeles, King of Swing Benny Goodman electrifies nationwide listeners with blazing swing classics including &#39;Sing, Sing, Sing&#39;, &#39;Bugle Call Rag&#39;, and dazzling Benny Goodman Quartet jazz improvisations for Camel Cigarettes.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Inspector_West_1970_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Beauty for Inspector West Part 5</code>, <code>Murder Wears a Veil</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Murder Wears a Veil (Part 5 — Patrick Barr as Inspector West — BBC)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1970-08-24<br>7:30 PM BST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>BBC Radio Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Patrick Barr</strong> (Inspector West), <strong>Avril Angers</strong>, <strong>John Hollis</strong></td>\n<td><strong>John Creasey</strong> (Author), <strong>Cynthia Pughe</strong>, <strong>John Browell</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;British&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Chief Inspector Roger &#39;Handsome&#39; West of Scotland Yard corners a ruthless extortion ring operating behind a high-fashion London beauty salon after a veiled blackmailer poisons a wealthy cosmetics magnate.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sentenced_1955_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>TCOT Juvenile Killer</code>, <code>Case Juvenile Killer Sentenced</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Juvenile Killer (Narrated by Jack Johnstone — Sentenced)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1955-08-24<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>True Crime Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>Jack Johnstone</strong> (Narrator), <strong>Karl Weber</strong>, <strong>Mandel Kramer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Sidney Marshall</strong> (Writer), <strong>Warren Somerville</strong>, <strong>Carl Caruso</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;True Crime&quot;, &quot;Documentary&quot;, &quot;Legal&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Real-life case files from state penitentiaries reconstruct the tragic trajectory of a teenage street-gang leader whose armed grocery robbery escalates into fatal manslaughter, culminating in a life imprisonment sentence and a sober warning to American youth.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Better_Half_1942_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Better Half 1942</code>, <code>Tiny Ruffner Marriage Quiz</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Battle of the Sexes: Husbands vs. Wives (Tiny Ruffner — Better Half)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1942-08-24<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Marriage Quiz Show</td>\n<td><strong>Tiny Ruffner</strong> (Quizmaster), <strong>Tom Slater</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual Radio Production</strong>, <strong>Herb Rice</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Quiz&quot;, &quot;Game Show&quot;, &quot;Marriage&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Audience Participation&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Jovial quizmaster Tiny Ruffner puts married couples to the ultimate battle-of-the-sexes test, quizzing husbands and wives on household chores, romantic trivia, and domestic habits for war stamps and prizes.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Better_Half_1944_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Better Half 1944</code>, <code>Wartime Husbands vs Wives</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Wartime Husbands vs. Wives (Tiny Ruffner — The Better Half)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1944-08-24<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Marriage Quiz Show</td>\n<td><strong>Tiny Ruffner</strong> (Quizmaster), <strong>Tom Slater</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual Radio Production</strong>, <strong>Herb Rice</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Quiz&quot;, &quot;Game Show&quot;, &quot;Marriage&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Audience Participation&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Tiny Ruffner hosts a lively wartime edition of the husband-versus-wife quiz show, asking military service wives and civilian husbands humorous questions regarding wartime victory gardening, rationing points, and budget management.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 216</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
