    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 32)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, syndication, and western radio history (1931–1964):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 32)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Claudia_1948_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>At The Ball Game</code>, <code>Claudia David Coca Cola</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;At the Ball Game (Starring Patricia Ryan &amp; Richard Kollmar — Coca-Cola)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndication</strong><br>1948-08-24<br>(WJZ New York)</td>\n<td><strong>The Coca-Cola Co.</strong><br>Coca-Cola / &quot;Coke&quot;</td>\n<td><strong>Patricia Ryan</strong> (Claudia), <strong>Richard Kollmar</strong> (David)</td>\n<td><strong>Rose Franken</strong>, <strong>William Brown Meloney</strong>, <strong>Joe King</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Marriage&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Newlyweds Claudia and David attend a lively afternoon baseball game at the polo grounds, where Claudia&#39;s complete misunderstanding of baseball rules and hilarious running commentary unwittingly distract both teams.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Death_Valley_1931_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Death Valley Night Club</code>, <code>Old Ranger 1931</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;A Death Valley Night Club (The Old Ranger — 20 Mule Team Borax)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1931-08-24<br>8:00 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Pacific Coast Borax</strong><br>20 Mule Team Borax</td>\n<td><strong>Tim Frawley</strong> (The Old Ranger), <strong>Joseph Bell</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ruth Cornwall Woodman</strong>, <strong>Edwin M. Whitney</strong>, <strong>George Hicks</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Old Ranger recounts the colorful true legend of an eccentric silver prospector who struck a bonanza lode and transformed an abandoned desert adobe outpost into the most opulent impromptu night club in the Nevada territory.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Death_Valley_1933_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Burro Hunt</code>, <code>Old Ranger 1933</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Burro Hunt (The Old Ranger — 20 Mule Team Borax)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1933-08-24<br>8:30 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Pacific Coast Borax</strong><br>20 Mule Team Borax</td>\n<td><strong>Tim Frawley</strong> (The Old Ranger), <strong>Jack MacBryde</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ruth Cornwall Woodman</strong>, <strong>Edwin M. Whitney</strong>, <strong>George Hicks</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Old Ranger spins the frontier tale of two stubborn desert prospectors whose lives are saved during a blinding Mojave dust storm when their stray pack burro leads them directly to an uncharted mountain spring.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Tide_Show_1945_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Tide Show Red Skelton</code>, <code>Junior Mean Widdle Kid</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Tide Show: Red Skelton (Junior the Mean Widdle Kid &amp; Tide)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WEAF)</strong><br>1945-08-24<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Tide Detergent</td>\n<td><strong>Red Skelton</strong>, <strong>Harriet Hilliard</strong>, <strong>Ozzie Nelson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Sherwood Schwartz</strong>, <strong>Keith McLeod</strong>, <strong>Rod O&#39;Connor</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Slapstick&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Red Skelton brings the house down with antics as Junior the &#39;Mean Widdle Kid&#39; (&#39;I dood it!&#39;) and country bumpkin Clem Kadiddlehopper, joined by Harriet Hilliard and David Rose&#39;s Orchestra for Tide Detergent.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Strange_Wills_1946_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Emeralds Come High</code>, <code>Warren William Strange Wills</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Emeralds Come High (Starring Warren William as John Francis O&#39;Connell)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Teleways Synd.</strong><br>1946-08-24<br>(KFI Los Angeles)</td>\n<td><strong>Regional Advertisers</strong><br>Commercial Sponsors</td>\n<td><strong>Warren William</strong> (John Francis O&#39;Connell), <strong>Howard Culver</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ken Krippene</strong> (Writer), <strong>C.P. MacGregor</strong>, <strong>Marvin Miller</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Legal&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Probate attorney John Francis O&#39;Connell investigates the bizarre last will and testament of an eccentric gem merchant who bequeaths a fortune in Colombian emeralds with a chilling condition: the heir must wear them in public despite knowing they carry a blood vendetta.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Theater_Five_1964_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>A Caller At Midnight</code>, <code>Theater Five Midnight Caller</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;A Caller at Midnight (Host Fred Foy — Theater Five)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WABC)</strong><br>1964-08-24<br>5:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>ABC Radio Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Fred Foy</strong> (Host), <strong>Robert Dryden</strong>, <strong>Teri Keane</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ted Bell</strong> (Producer/Director), <strong>George Lowther</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Suspense&quot;, &quot;Thriller&quot;, &quot;Psychological&quot;, &quot;Audio Drama&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>A solitary woman alone in a secluded hillside cottage receives a series of increasingly menacing phone calls at midnight from an unseen intruder who describes her every movement from just outside the window.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 192</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
