    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 30)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, daytime drama, and military morale history (1933–1959):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 30)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Johnny_Mercer_1944_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Exactly Like You 1944</code>, <code>Mercer Stafford Old Gold</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Exactly Like You &amp; Ac-Cent-Tchu-Ate the Positive (Johnny Mercer — Old Gold)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WEAF)</strong><br>1944-08-24<br>10:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>P. Lorillard Company</strong><br>Old Gold Cigarettes</td>\n<td><strong>Johnny Mercer</strong>, <strong>Jo Stafford</strong>, <strong>The Pied Pipers</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Paul Weston Orchestra</strong>, <strong>Howard Wiley</strong>, <strong>Doug Gourlay</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Swing&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Johnny Mercer and Jo Stafford team up for a joyful evening of musical comedy, delivering toe-tapping swing interpretations of &#39;Exactly Like You&#39;, &#39;Ac-Cent-Tchu-Ate the Positive&#39;, and &#39;G.I. Jive&#39; for Old Gold Cigarettes.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Man_Named_Jordan_1952_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode 8</code>, <code>The Istanbul Connection</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Istanbul Relic (Episode 8 — Jack Moyles as Rocky Jordan — Del Monte)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS West Coast</strong><br>1952-08-24<br>6:30 PM PDT</td>\n<td><strong>Del Monte Foods</strong><br>Canned Fruits &amp; Veggies</td>\n<td><strong>Jack Moyles</strong> (Rocky Jordan), <strong>Jay Novello</strong></td>\n<td><strong>G.K. Breitenstein &amp; Larry Roman</strong>, <strong>Cliff Howell</strong>, <strong>Larry Thor</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Noir&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Exotic&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Istanbul, world-weary American expatriate café owner Rocky Jordan protects an endangered archaeologist from a ruthless black-market antiquity ring determined to seize a priceless Byzantine relic.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Rudy_Vallee_1933_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Little Minister Helen Hayes</code>, <code>Fleischmanns Yeast Hour 1933</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Little Minister (Starring Helen Hayes with Rudy Vallee — Fleischmann&#39;s Yeast)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Red (WEAF)</strong><br>1933-08-24<br>8:00 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Standard Brands</strong><br>Fleischmann&#39;s Yeast for Health</td>\n<td><strong>Rudy Vallee</strong>, <strong>Helen Hayes</strong> (Babbie), <strong>John Griggs</strong></td>\n<td><strong>J.M. Barrie</strong> (Author), <strong>Graham McNamee</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Adaptation&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Host Rudy Vallee welcomes Broadway and Hollywood luminary Helen Hayes to perform scenes from J.M. Barrie&#39;s Scottish romantic drama <em>The Little Minister</em>, complemented by crooning favorites and jazz selections by The Connecticut Yankees for Fleischmann&#39;s Yeast.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Rudy_Vallee_1939_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Guest Jimmy Durante</code>, <code>Royal Gelatin Hour Durante</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Royal Gelatin Hour: Guest Jimmy Durante (Rudy Vallee)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Red (WEAF)</strong><br>1939-08-24<br>8:00 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Standard Brands</strong><br>Royal Gelatin &amp; Puddings</td>\n<td><strong>Rudy Vallee</strong>, <strong>Jimmy Durante</strong> (Guest Star)</td>\n<td><strong>J. Walter Thompson</strong>, <strong>Graham McNamee</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Slapstick&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Inka Dinka Doo!&quot; Schnozzola himself Jimmy Durante storms the Rudy Vallee stage for a riotous half-hour of piano-smashing songs, rapid-fire dialect jokes, and chaotic comedic banter with Vallee and The Connecticut Yankees for Royal Gelatin.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Forever_Tops_1959_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Paul Martel</code>, <code>Paul Whiteman AFRTS 1959</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Forever Tops #22: Symphonic Jazz Masters (Paul Whiteman — AFRTS)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AFRTS Los Angeles</strong><br>1959-08-24<br>(Show #22)</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Armed Forces Morale</td>\n<td><strong>Paul Whiteman and his Orchestra</strong>, <strong>Earl Wrightson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AFRTS Production</strong>, <strong>Doug Gourlay</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Jazz&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;, &quot;Orchestral&quot;, &quot;Nostalgia&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The King of Jazz Paul Whiteman leads his magnificent symphonic jazz orchestra through timeless orchestral pop masterpieces, spotlighting soaring arrangements of &#39;Rhapsody in Blue&#39;, &#39;Whispering&#39;, and &#39;Smoke Gets in Your Eyes&#39; for American service personnel overseas.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Ma_Perkins_1950_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Ma Asks Evie Life Savings</code>, <code>Ma Perkins Oxydol 1950</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Evie and the Family Savings (Starring Virginia Payne as Ma Perkins — Oxydol)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1950-08-24<br>1:15 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Oxydol Detergent</td>\n<td><strong>Virginia Payne</strong> (Ma Perkins), <strong>Laurette Fillbrandt</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Robert Hardy Andrews</strong>, <strong>Orin Tovrov</strong>, <strong>Dick Wells</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Soap Opera&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Rushville Center, lumberyard matriarch Ma Perkins confronts her distraught daughter Evie, desperately inquiring whether she handed over their hard-earned family life savings to smooth-talking Sylvester under false pretenses.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 180</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
