    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 12)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, Canadian CBC Radio, and British BBC Light Programme broadcasting history (1947–1982):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 12)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Midnight_1982_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Second Sunday In May</code>, <code>Timothy Findley CBC 1982</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Second Sunday in May (Timothy Findley Drama — CBC Midnight)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBC Radio</strong><br>1982-08-24<br>11:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBC Radio Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Neil Munro</strong>, <strong>Nonnie Griffin</strong>, <strong>Tony Van Bridge</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Timothy Findley</strong> (Writer), <strong>John Douglas</strong>, <strong>Bill Hawes</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Psychological&quot;, &quot;Thriller&quot;, &quot;Canadian&quot;, &quot;Suspense&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In a dark psychological drama, an estranged son returns to his family&#39;s remote Ontario estate on Mother&#39;s Day, reopening unresolved traumas and uncovering a chilling secret hidden in his mother&#39;s locked bedroom.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Floggits_1956_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode 02 - Tree Problems</code>, <code>Gert and Daisy Floggit</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Floggits: Tree Problems (Gert &amp; Daisy — BBC Light Programme)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Light Prog.</strong><br>1956-08-24<br>8:00 PM BST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>BBC Light Programme</td>\n<td><strong>Elsie Waters</strong>, <strong>Doris Waters</strong>, <strong>Joan Sims</strong>, <strong>Ronnie Barker</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Terry Nation &amp; John Junkin</strong>, <strong>Bill Worsley</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;British&quot;, &quot;Humor&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Gert and Daisy Floggit attempt to trim an overgrown ancient oak tree threatening the roof of their general store in the sleepy village of Rushey Green, causing hilarious chaos for the local constable and town council.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Barrie_Craig_1954_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Blood Money</code>, <code>William Gargan Barrie Craig</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Blood Money (Starring William Gargan as Barrie Craig — Confidential Investigator)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1954-08-24<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC Mystery Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>William Gargan</strong> (Barrie Craig), <strong>Ralph Bell</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Louis Vittes</strong> (Writer), <strong>Himan Brown</strong>, <strong>Don Pardo</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Noir&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Manhattan private investigator Barrie Craig is offered ten thousand dollars in blood-soaked banknotes to locate a missing underworld courier before rival syndicate hitmen track him down at an abandoned Hudson River ferry slip.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>NBC_Theater_1959_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Cinderella</code>, <code>Madeleine Carroll Fairy Godmother</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Cinderella (Narrated by Madeleine Carroll — NBC Radio Theater)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1959-08-24<br>10:05 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC Dramatic Series</td>\n<td><strong>Madeleine Carroll</strong> (Narrator), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong>, <strong>Karl Swenson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>George Lefferts</strong> (Adaptation), <strong>Fred Collins</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Fantasy&quot;, &quot;Fairy Tale&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Screen star Madeleine Carroll narrates a lyrical radio dramatization of <em>Cinderella</em>, following the mistreated scullery maid whose magical glass slipper leads the Prince to her doorstep after the royal stroke of midnight.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Under_Arrest_1947_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Counterfeit Diamonds</code>, <code>Joe DeSantis Drake</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Counterfeit Diamonds (Starring Joe DeSantis as Captain Drake)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1947-08-24<br>5:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Police Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Joe DeSantis</strong> (Captain Drake), <strong>Ted de Corsia</strong></td>\n<td><strong>William Sweets</strong> (Writer), <strong>Martin Gabel</strong>, <strong>Jimmy Blaine</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Police Captain John Drake unravels a diamond merchant&#39;s staged burglary scam, using microscopic gem analysis to prove the jeweler swapped genuine flawless diamonds for paste before filing an insurance claim.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Under_Arrest_1952_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Waterfront Hijackers</code>, <code>Craig McDonnell Scott</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Waterfront Hijackers (Starring Craig McDonnell as Captain Scott)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1952-08-24<br>5:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Police Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Craig McDonnell</strong> (Captain Scott), <strong>Larry Haines</strong></td>\n<td><strong>William Sweets</strong> (Writer), <strong>Martin Gabel</strong>, <strong>Jimmy Blaine</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Police Captain Jim Scott leads a squad of harbor precinct detectives in an undercover stakeout to bust an armed hijacking ring raiding bonded whiskey warehouses along the Brooklyn piers.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 72</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
