    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 04)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network and AFRS military broadcasting history (1943–1951):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 04)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>ILAM_1943_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Murder Is Word Part 12</code>, <code>ILAM Ivory Soap 1943</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Murder Is the Word for It (Chapter 12 — Ivory Soap)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1943-08-24<br>7:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Ivory Soap &amp; Oxydol</td>\n<td><strong>Michael Raffetto</strong> (Jack), <strong>Barton Yarborough</strong> (Doc)</td>\n<td><strong>Carlton E. Morse</strong> (Author/Director), <strong>Frank Martin</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In chapter twelve of <em>Murder Is the Word for It</em>, Jack Packard and Doc Long discover the decapitated body of an heiress hidden behind a sliding bookshelf in an isolated mountain mansion, realizing the murderer is trapped in the house with them.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ILAM_1944_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Temple Vampires Part 3</code>, <code>Mercedes McCambridge ILAM</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Temple of Vampires (Chapter 3 — Ivory Soap)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1944-08-24<br>7:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Ivory Soap &amp; Oxydol</td>\n<td><strong>Michael Raffetto</strong> (Jack), <strong>Barton Yarborough</strong>, <strong>Mercedes McCambridge</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Carlton E. Morse</strong> (Author/Director), <strong>Frank Martin</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In chapter three of <em>The Temple of Vampires</em>, Jack, Doc, and Reggie navigate a treacherous subterranean tunnel beneath a ruined Mayan temple in Nicaragua, finding themselves encircled by blood-drinking bats and hooded cultists.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ILAM_1950_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Turquoise Pass Part 4</code>, <code>Russell Thorson Tony Randall</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Murder in Turquoise Pass (Chapter 4 — Starring Russell Thorson &amp; Tony Randall)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1950-08-24<br>7:45 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Mystery Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>Russell Thorson</strong> (Jack), <strong>Jim Boles</strong> (Doc), <strong>Tony Randall</strong> (Reggie)</td>\n<td><strong>Carlton E. Morse</strong> (Author/Director), <strong>Ed Michael</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In chapter four of <em>Murder in Turquoise Pass</em>, the A-1 Detective Agency trio track an armed gang of gold hijackers through an abandoned Arizona copper mine, dodging dynamite booby-traps rigged along the mine tracks.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ILAM_1951_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Hollywood Style Part 10</code>, <code>ILAM Mutual 1951</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Murder Hollywood Style (Chapter 10 — Starring Russell Thorson &amp; Tony Randall)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1951-08-24<br>7:45 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Mystery Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>Russell Thorson</strong> (Jack), <strong>Jim Boles</strong> (Doc), <strong>Tony Randall</strong> (Reggie)</td>\n<td><strong>Carlton E. Morse</strong> (Author/Director), <strong>Ed Michael</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In chapter ten of <em>Murder Hollywood Style</em>, Jack and Doc confront a blackmailing movie studio publicist on a dark soundstage catwalk, narrowly escaping a lethal fall when a high-voltage studio spotlight is hurled at them.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Call_Police_1948_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Perfumed Grand</code>, <code>Commissioner Grant Rinso</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Perfumed Grand (Starring Joseph Julian as Commissioner Grant — Rinso)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1948-08-24<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Lever Brothers</strong><br>Rinso Soap Powder &amp; Lifebuoy</td>\n<td><strong>Joseph Julian</strong> (Bill Grant), <strong>Amzie Strickland</strong>, <strong>Robert Dryden</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Peter Barry</strong> (Writer), <strong>Carlo De Angelo</strong>, <strong>Jay Jostyn</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Police Commissioner Bill Grant investigates the murder of a high-stakes illegal racetrack gambler whose pockets were stuffed with scented thousand-dollar banknotes, tracing the distinctive floral perfume to an exclusive Park Avenue salon.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>AFRS_1946_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>To The Rear March</code>, <code>Burgess Meredith Mel Blanc</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;To the Rear, March! Post-War Veterans Special (Burgess Meredith &amp; Mel Blanc)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AFRS Unit</strong><br>1946-08-24<br>(Demobilization Series)</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. War Dept</strong><br>Armed Forces Radio Service</td>\n<td><strong>Burgess Meredith</strong> (Host), <strong>Mel Blanc</strong>, <strong>Alan Reed</strong>, <strong>Frank Nelson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Jerome Lawrence &amp; Robert E. Lee</strong>, <strong>Hy Averback</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Docudrama&quot;, &quot;Military&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Morale&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Actor Burgess Meredith hosts an entertaining post-war military broadcast providing crucial demobilization, G.I. Bill education rights, and civilian readjustment advice to returning WWII servicemen through humorous sketches featuring Mel Blanc.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 24</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
