    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 63)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American network, syndication, and South African broadcasting history (1943–1968):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 63)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Howard_Miller_1957_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Bob Jaxson</code>, <code>Howard Miller Bob Jaxon</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Howard Miller Show with Guest Bob Jaxon (CBS Radio — WBBM Chicago)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WBBM)</strong><br>1957-08-23<br>10:45 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Wrigley&#39;s Gum</strong><br>Wrigley&#39;s Spearmint Gum</td>\n<td><strong>Howard Miller</strong> (Host / DJ), <strong>Bob Jaxon</strong> (Guest)</td>\n<td><strong>WBBM Chicago / CBS Radio Presentation</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Interview&quot;, &quot;Pop&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Disc jockey Howard Miller chats with rising young RCA Victor recording artist Bob Jaxon, spinning Jaxon&#39;s latest pop singles and discussing teenage jukebox trends across the Midwest.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Wayside_Theater_1943_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode</code>, <code>The Road to Elmira</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Road to Elmira (Starring Donald Woods &amp; Frances Chaney — Wayside Theater)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Red (WEAF)</strong><br>1943-08-23<br>9:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC Summer Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Donald Woods</strong>, <strong>Frances Chaney</strong>, <strong>Karl Swenson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>George Faulkner</strong> (Writer), <strong>Lester Vail</strong>, <strong>Jack Costello</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Small Town&quot;, &quot;Morale&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>A heartwarming small-town wartime drama about a weary big-city commercial artist stranded in an upstate New York village, where he helps an earnest young woman save her family&#39;s struggling roadside inn.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>On_Safari_1968_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Big Dutch Last Safari</code>, <code>On Safari Final Episode</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Big Dutch&#39;s Last Safari (Series Finale — On Safari)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>SABC English</strong><br>1968-08-23<br>(South Africa)</td>\n<td><strong>Commercial Sponsors</strong><br>SABC English Service</td>\n<td><strong>Tommy Read</strong> (Big Dutch), <strong>Colin Fish</strong>, <strong>Patrick Mynhardt</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Tommy Read</strong> (Writer/Producer), <strong>Bruce Stewart</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Outdoors&quot;, &quot;African&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In the dramatic final adventure of the series, veteran white hunter Big Dutch leads his last safari deep into the uncharted Zambezi bushveld to rescue stranded geologists from a ring of diamond smugglers before retiring from the bush.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Dunninger_1944_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Dunninger Kem-Tone 1944</code>, <code>Master Mentalist</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Dunninger The Master Mentalist (Kem-Tone Miracle Wall Paint)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blue Network (WJZ)</strong><br>1944-08-23<br>9:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sherwin-Williams</strong><br>Kem-Tone Miracle Wall Paint</td>\n<td><strong>Joseph Dunninger</strong> (The Mentalist), <strong>Bill Slater</strong> (MC)</td>\n<td><strong>Roger White</strong> (Producer), <strong>Earl McGill</strong>, <strong>Glenn Riggs</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Mentalism&quot;, &quot;Magic&quot;, &quot;Quiz&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Master mentalist Joseph Dunninger astounds radio listeners and a panel of skeptical celebrity judges by reading sealed thoughts from locked steel boxes and reproducing hidden serial numbers from dollar bills over the air for Kem-Tone Paint.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Chick_Carter_1943_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>X24- Rattlers Emergency</code>, <code>Chick Carter Episode 74</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Rattler&#39;s Emergency Order (Chick Carter, Boy Detective — Episode #74)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1943-08-23<br>5:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Street &amp; Smith</strong><br>Street &amp; Smith Youth Mystery</td>\n<td><strong>Leon Janney</strong> (Chick Carter), <strong>Bill Lipton</strong>, <strong>Joanne Myers</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Fritz Blocki</strong> (Writer), <strong>Lawrence Holcomb</strong>, <strong>Ken Powell</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Pulp&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In the thrilling serial storyline, young sleuth Chick Carter intercepts a coded telegraph dispatch from criminal mastermind The Rattler, racing against time to prevent the sabotage of an experimental munitions shipment.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Chick_Carter_1944_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Black Falcon</code>, <code>Chick Carter Episode 335</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Trap of the Black Falcon (Chick Carter, Boy Detective — Episode #335)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1944-08-23<br>5:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Street &amp; Smith</strong><br>Street &amp; Smith Youth Mystery</td>\n<td><strong>Leon Janney</strong> (Chick Carter), <strong>Bill Lipton</strong>, <strong>Gilbert Mack</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Fritz Blocki</strong> (Writer), <strong>Lawrence Holcomb</strong>, <strong>Ken Powell</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Pulp&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Continuing the serial mystery, Chick Carter and his loyal companion Tex Fletcher discover a secret underground printing press used by counterfeiter &#39;The Black Falcon&#39;, only to be trapped inside a steel vault as the room fills with water.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 378</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
