    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 45)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across the Golden Age of <em>The Lone Ranger</em> on American network radio (1940–1954):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 45)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Lone_Ranger_1940_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Brothers</code>, <code>Range War Averted</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Brothers: A Range War Averted (Bond Bread)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>WXYZ / Mutual</strong><br>1940-08-23<br>7:30 PM EST</td>\n<td><strong>General Baking Co.</strong><br>Bond Bread</td>\n<td><strong>Earle Graser</strong> (Lone Ranger), <strong>John Todd</strong> (Tonto)</td>\n<td><strong>Fran Striker</strong> (Writer), <strong>Charles Livingstone</strong>, <strong>Fred Foy</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Lone Ranger and Tonto intervene in a deadly frontier dispute between two estranged rancher brothers who are being manipulated into a bloody range war by a scheming land speculator.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Lone_Ranger_1943_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>A Good Womans Love</code>, <code>Lone Ranger Cheerios 1943</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;A Good Woman&#39;s Love: Reforming a Gunslinger (Cheerios &amp; Kix)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blue Network (WJZ)</strong><br>1943-08-23<br>7:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>General Mills Inc.</strong><br>Cheerios &amp; Kix Cereal</td>\n<td><strong>Brace Beemer</strong> (Lone Ranger), <strong>John Todd</strong> (Tonto)</td>\n<td><strong>Fran Striker</strong> (Writer), <strong>Charles Livingstone</strong>, <strong>Fred Foy</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Lone Ranger aids a courageous frontier schoolteacher in her efforts to reform a wayward young gunslinger before a gang of ruthless bank robbers forces him back into a life of crime.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Lone_Ranger_1944_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Tricky</code>, <code>Counterfeit Horse Trader</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Tricky: The Counterfeit Horse Trader (Cheerios &amp; Wheaties)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blue Network (WJZ)</strong><br>1944-08-23<br>7:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>General Mills</strong><br>Cheerios &amp; Wheaties</td>\n<td><strong>Brace Beemer</strong> (Lone Ranger), <strong>John Todd</strong> (Tonto)</td>\n<td><strong>Fran Striker</strong> (Writer), <strong>Charles Livingstone</strong>, <strong>Fred Foy</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Lone Ranger and Tonto expose a deceptive frontier horse trader whose counterfeit bills and stolen thoroughbred stock are part of an interstate smuggling ring.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Lone_Ranger_1946_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Stubborn Man</code>, <code>The Stubborn Homesteader</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Stubborn Homesteader (Cheerios)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1946-08-23<br>7:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>General Mills</strong><br>Cheerios Cereal</td>\n<td><strong>Brace Beemer</strong> (Lone Ranger), <strong>John Todd</strong> (Tonto)</td>\n<td><strong>Fran Striker</strong> (Writer), <strong>Charles Livingstone</strong>, <strong>Fred Foy</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Lone Ranger and Tonto ride to protect an obstinate homesteader who refuses to leave his fertile valley homestead despite violent intimidation and night-riding arson attacks by a corrupt water baron.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Lone_Ranger_1950_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Feud on the Range</code>, <code>The Range Feud 1950</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Feud on the Range (Cheerios &amp; Wheaties)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1950-08-23<br>7:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>General Mills</strong><br>Cheerios &amp; Wheaties</td>\n<td><strong>Brace Beemer</strong> (Lone Ranger), <strong>John Todd</strong> (Tonto)</td>\n<td><strong>Fran Striker</strong> (Writer), <strong>Charles Livingstone</strong>, <strong>Fred Foy</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Lone Ranger and Tonto prevent bloodshed in a volatile range war between sheep herders and cattle barons, revealing that an ambitious outlaw gang provoked the feud to seize grazing lands for themselves.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Lone_Ranger_1954_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Dead Man</code>, <code>The Dead Mans Trail 1954</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Dead Man&#39;s Trail (Cheerios)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WABC)</strong><br>1954-08-23<br>7:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>General Mills</strong><br>Cheerios Cereal</td>\n<td><strong>Brace Beemer</strong> (Lone Ranger), <strong>John Todd</strong> (Tonto)</td>\n<td><strong>Fran Striker</strong> (Writer), <strong>Charles Livingstone</strong>, <strong>Fred Foy</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Lone Ranger tracks an elusive escaped convict who staged his own death in a desert mine collapse, exposing his disguise as a respectable frontier town banker before he can loot the town vault.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 270</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
