    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 42)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American network, military, and syndicated broadcasting history (1943–1953):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 42)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Richard_Diamond_1950_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Rich 063 Insurance Matter</code>, <code>Ralph Evans Insurance</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Ralph Evans Insurance Fraud Case (Starring Dick Powell — Rexall)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1950-08-23<br>10:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Rexall Drug Co.</strong><br>Rexall 1-Cent Sale &amp; Plenamins</td>\n<td><strong>Dick Powell</strong> (Richard Diamond), <strong>Virginia Gregg</strong>, <strong>Ed Begley</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blake Edwards</strong> (Writer/Creator), <strong>Jaime del Valle</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Singing private eye Richard Diamond is hired by an anxious insurance company when a wealthy client dies under suspicious circumstances shortly after purchasing an enormous life insurance policy, leading Diamond into an elaborate blackmail and murder conspiracy.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Richard_Diamond_1950_08_23_2.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Evans Farmer Case</code>, <code>Evans Farmer Fraud</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Evans Farmer Case (Starring Dick Powell — Rexall)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1950-08-23<br>10:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Rexall Drug Co.</strong><br>Rexall Drug Products</td>\n<td><strong>Dick Powell</strong> (Richard Diamond), <strong>Virginia Gregg</strong>, <strong>Ed Begley</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blake Edwards</strong> (Writer), <strong>Jaime del Valle</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Private detective Richard Diamond investigates a fraudulent farm insurance claim involving a faked tractor fatality, cracking wise with Lieutenant Levinson while uncovering a rural homicide ring.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Richard_Diamond_1953_08_23_AFRTS.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Rich 153 Hollywood Story</code>, <code>Hollywood Starlet Murder</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Hollywood Story (AFRTS #153 — Starring Dick Powell)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AFRTS / CBS</strong><br>1953-08-23<br>7:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>Armed Forces Radio Service</td>\n<td><strong>Dick Powell</strong> (Richard Diamond), <strong>Virginia Gregg</strong>, <strong>Arthur Q. Bryan</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blake Edwards</strong> (Writer), <strong>Bob Lemond</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Richard Diamond navigates the glamour and underworld vice of Hollywood after a terrified starlet begs for protection from an obsessive stalker, only for Diamond to find his client poisoned inside her dressing room.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Richard_Diamond_1953_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Rich 155 Hollywood Story</code>, <code>Dick Powell Richard Diamond</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Hollywood Story: The Murder of a Movie Starlet (Starring Dick Powell)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1953-08-23<br>7:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Mystery Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>Dick Powell</strong> (Richard Diamond), <strong>Virginia Gregg</strong>, <strong>Arthur Q. Bryan</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blake Edwards</strong> (Writer), <strong>Jaime del Valle</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Private investigator Richard Diamond takes a case in the movie industry to shield a rising film actress from an extortionist, dodging hired thugs on studio soundstages before serenading Helen at the piano.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Eyes_Aloft_1943_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Eyes Aloft 1943</code>, <code>Aircraft Warning Service</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Eyes Aloft: Vigil on the Pacific Coast (USAAF Fourth Fighter Command)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Pacific (KFI)</strong><br>1943-08-23<br>6:00 PM PWT</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Army Air Forces</strong><br>Aircraft Warning Service</td>\n<td><strong>Lurene Tuttle</strong>, <strong>Elliott Lewis</strong>, <strong>Frank Graham</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Robert Tallman</strong> (Writer), <strong>True Boardman</strong>, <strong>Ken Niles</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Docudrama&quot;, &quot;War&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Military&quot;, &quot;Aviation&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Dramatizing real-life wartime vigilance along the Pacific Coast, civilian spotters at a remote observation post in the Sierra Nevada mountains coordinate with the U.S. Army Fourth Fighter Command to track and intercept an unidentified distress flight.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Serenade_Blue_1953_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Im Going To Love That Guy</code>, <code>Serenade in Blue 342</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Serenade in Blue #342: The United States Air Force Band &amp; Singing Sergeants&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndication</strong><br>1953-08-23<br>(Transcribed)</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Air Force</strong><br>Air Force Recruiting</td>\n<td><strong>USAF Band &amp; Singing Sergeants</strong>, <strong>Maj. George S. Howard</strong></td>\n<td><strong>USAF Directorate of PR</strong>, <strong>M/Sgt Arthur Sparkman</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Military&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Major George S. Howard conducts The United States Air Force Band and The Singing Sergeants in a patriotic musical showcase for Air Force recruiting, performing &#39;I&#39;m Gonna Love That Guy&#39; and &#39;The U.S. Air Force Song&#39;.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 252</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
