    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 15)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, serial multi-part narrative arcs, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American network and syndication broadcasting history (1946–1956):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 15)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Champion_1949_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Mystery Lost Treasure Ch 2</code>, <code>Champion Western Serial</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Mystery of the Lost Treasure (Chapter 2) — Superstition Mountain&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual</strong><br>1949-08-23<br>5:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Juvenile Western Series</td>\n<td><strong>Gene Autry</strong>, <strong>Johnny Bond</strong>, <strong>Pat Buttram</strong>, <strong>Champion</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arthur Browne Jr.</strong> (Writer), <strong>Frank Bingham</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Children&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 2 of <em>The Mystery of the Lost Treasure</em>, Gene Autry and his wonder horse Champion track outlaw claim-jumpers into Superstition Mountain, rescuing a young Navajo boy trapped on a crumbling canyon ledge.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Philo_Vance_1949_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Blue Penny Murder Case</code>, <code>Mauritius Stamp Forgery</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Blue Penny Murder Case (Starring Jackson Beck)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ziv Syndication</strong><br>1949-08-23<br>(WNBC / Syndicated)</td>\n<td><strong>Local Commercials</strong><br>Co-op Advertisers</td>\n<td><strong>Jackson Beck</strong> (Philo Vance), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong>, <strong>George Petrie</strong></td>\n<td><strong>S.S. Van Dine</strong> (Author), <strong>Frederic W. Ziv</strong> (Director), <strong>Kenny Delmar</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Aristocratic sleuth Philo Vance is called in when an eccentric stamp collector is found murdered inside his locked vault, discovering that a world-famous 1847 Mauritius &#39;Blue Penny&#39; postage stamp was switched with an expert forgery.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Official_Detective_1949_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Night Watchman Murder</code>, <code>Chemical Plant Safe Robbery</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Murder of the Night Watchman (Detective Lt. Dan Britton)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1949-08-23<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Radio Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Craig McDonnell</strong> (Lt. Dan Britton), <strong>Tom Tully</strong>, <strong>Mandel Kramer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>William Sweets</strong> (Writer), <strong>Wynn Wright</strong> (Director), <strong>Carl Warren</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;True Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Detective Lieutenant Dan Britton investigates the bludgeoning of an elderly night watchman at a chemical plant, reconstructing tire tread impressions to trap a gang of industrial saboteurs.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Official_Detective_1956_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Highway Hijackers</code>, <code>Turnpike Armored Car Heist</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Highway Turnpike Hijackers (Detective Lt. Dan Britton)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1956-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Radio Series</td>\n<td><strong>Craig McDonnell</strong> (Lt. Dan Britton), <strong>Lawson Zerbe</strong>, <strong>Ralph Bell</strong></td>\n<td><strong>William Sweets</strong> (Writer), <strong>Wynn Wright</strong> (Director), <strong>Carl Warren</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;True Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Lieutenant Dan Britton coordinates an interstate roadblock operation after a ruthless highway robbery crew hijacks an armored jewelry transport van along the Pennsylvania Turnpike.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sam_Spade_1946_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Zig Zags of Treachery</code>, <code>Zigzag Treachery Caper</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Zig Zags of Treachery Caper (Wildroot Cream-Oil)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1946-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Wildroot Co., Inc.</strong><br>Wildroot Cream-Oil Hair Tonic</td>\n<td><strong>Howard Duff</strong> (Sam Spade), <strong>Lurene Tuttle</strong> (Effie), <strong>William Conrad</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bob Tallman &amp; Jason James</strong> (Writers), <strong>William Spier</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Noir&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Private investigator Sam Spade is hired by an elusive femme fatale who claims her ex-husband is trying to kill her, leading Spade through a maze of double-crosses across San Francisco&#39;s fog-shrouded wharves to uncover a hidden bullion fortune.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Ethel_And_Albert_1946_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Albert Phones From California</code>, <code>Cross Country Phone Call</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Albert Phones Long Distance from California (Peg Lynch &amp; Alan Bunce)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1946-08-23<br>2:15 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>ABC Daytime Sitcom</td>\n<td><strong>Peg Lynch</strong> (Ethel Arbuckle), <strong>Alan Bunce</strong> (Albert Arbuckle)</td>\n<td><strong>Peg Lynch</strong> (Creator &amp; Writer), <strong>Bob Brown</strong> (Director), <strong>Fred Cole</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Marriage&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>While Albert is attending a business convention in Los Angeles, Ethel frantically prepares for his expensive long-distance phone call home to Sandy Harbor, only to spend three costly minutes debating the correct spelling of an aunt&#39;s recipe ingredient.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 90</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
