    "html": "<h2>August 22 100% Archival Metadata Completion Milestone</h2>\n<p>With this dispatch, <strong>August 22nd has achieved 100% archival cataloging completion (233/233 broadcasts resolved)</strong>. Every broadcast airing on August 22 across recorded radio history now possesses canonical titles, verified airtimes, network attribution, commercial sponsorships, credited cast and characters, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, standardized taxonomy genres, and story-first narrative synopses.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>Final August 22 Archival Inventory</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Blair_Mounties_1935_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode 4</code>, <code>Yukon Fur Poachers</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Inspector Blair and the Yukon Fur Poachers (Chapter 4)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Transco Syndication</strong><br>1935-08-22<br>(Hollywood)</td>\n<td><strong>Regional Advertisers</strong><br>Dairy &amp; Bakery Sponsors</td>\n<td><strong>Col. Arthur P. Kelly</strong> (Inspector Blair, RCMP)</td>\n<td><strong>Arthur P. Kelly</strong> (Writer), Transco Radio Transcriptions</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Inspector Blair of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police mushing through a blinding Yukon blizzard tracks an armed fur poacher to a barricaded trading outpost, outwitting the fugitive before the fresh trail is wiped out.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Monte_Cristo_1944_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Chateau d&#39;If Escape</code>, <code>Monte Cristo 1944</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Escape from the Chateau d&#39;If &amp; the Treasure of Monte Cristo&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1944-08-22<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Drama Series</td>\n<td><strong>Carleton Young</strong> (Edmond Dantès), <strong>Parley Baer</strong> (Ali), <strong>Betty Lou Gerson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Alexandre Dumas</strong> (Author), <strong>Martin Magner</strong> (Adapter), <strong>Jaime del Valle</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Literature&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Imprisoned unjustly for fourteen years in the dreaded Chateau d&#39;If dungeon, Edmond Dantès executes a daring escape inside a burial shroud, retrieving the legendary Spada treasure on the Isle of Monte Cristo to launch his quest for vengeance.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Monte_Cristo_1950_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Deaf and Blind Witnesses</code>, <code>Paris Carriage Murder</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Deaf and Blind Witnesses&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1950-08-22<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Adventure Series</td>\n<td><strong>Carleton Young</strong> (Edmond Dantès), <strong>Virginia Gregg</strong>, <strong>Parley Baer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Martin Magner</strong> (Writer), <strong>Jaime del Valle</strong> (Director), <strong>Don McCall</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In 19th-century Paris, Edmond Dantès investigates the carriage assassination of a prominent French magistrate, solving the homicide by coordinating the sensory testimonies of a deaf lip-reader who saw the assassin&#39;s words and a blind violinist who heard the killer&#39;s footsteps.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>August 22 Completion Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 22</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved on August 22</strong>: 233 / 233 (100.0% Complete)</li>\n<li><strong>Total Dispatches Published for August 22</strong>: 37 (Walks 01–37)</li>\n<li><strong>Status</strong>: August 22 completely finished. Proceeding sequentially to <strong>August 23rd</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n",
