    "html": "<h2>Batch 81 Forensic Discoveries</h2>\n<p>Batch 81 recovers and dates 9 historical broadcasts spanning classic network comedy sketches, family sitcoms, early morning southwestern string band programs, celebrity sports interviews, and magazine dramatizations: 2 vintage 1948 broadcasts from Red Skelton on <em><strong>The Red Skelton Show</strong></em> (featuring Junior the Mean Widdle Kid and Clem Kadiddlehopper), Arthur Lake and Penny Singleton in <em><strong>Blondie</strong></em> (1944), Bill Stern interviewing Hollywood superstar Lucille Ball and tennis champion Jack Kramer on AFRS <em><strong>Sports Newsreel</strong></em> (1946–1947), 3 rare broadcasts from Mineral Wells, Texas sponsored by <em><strong>Crazy Water Crystals</strong></em> (1935–1958), and true confession drama on <em><strong>Modern Romances</strong></em> (1950).</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>The Red Skelton Show</em> &amp; <em>Blondie</em> (1944–1948)</h2>\n<p>Beloved network comedy characters:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Verified Airdate</th>\n<th>Comedy Characters &amp; Narrative</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Red_Skelton_Junior_Zoo.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Red Skelton Show: &#39;Junior the Mean Widdle Kid Goes to the Zoo&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1948-03-09</strong></td>\n<td>Junior wreaks havoc among the exotic animals.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Red_Skelton_Clem_Department.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Red Skelton Show: &#39;Clem Kadiddlehopper at the Department Store&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1948-03-23</strong></td>\n<td>Clem encounters revolving doors, escalators, and exasperated clerks.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Blondie_Missing_Package.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Blondie: &#39;Dagwood&#39;s Missing Package &amp; The Secret Formula&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1944-10-01</strong></td>\n<td>Dagwood misplaces an important architectural blueprint package.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Bill Stern&#39;s Sports Newsreel</em>, <em>Crazy Water</em>, &amp; <em>Modern Romances</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Verified Airdate</th>\n<th>Broadcast Substance</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Sports_Newsreel_Lucille_Ball.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;AFRS Sports Newsreel: Bill Stern interviews Lucille Ball&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1946-09-27</strong></td>\n<td>Lucille Ball discusses tennis, athletic conditioning, and Hollywood life.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sports_Newsreel_Jack_Kramer.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;AFRS Sports Newsreel: Bill Stern interviews Jack Kramer &amp; Bill Schroeder&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1947-06-13</strong></td>\n<td>US Tennis Champion Jack Kramer previewing international championship play.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Crazy_Water_Hotel_Prog_12.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Crazy Water Crystals: &#39;Live from the Crazy Water Hotel&#39; (Prog 12)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1935-08-14</strong></td>\n<td>Early southwestern hillbilly string band music from Mineral Wells, Texas.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Crazy_Water_Hotel_Prog_17.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Crazy Water Crystals: &#39;The Sunshine Special of Health and Happiness&#39; (Prog 17)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1935-09-18</strong></td>\n<td>High-energy fiddle tunes, gospel quartets, and country humor.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Crazy_Water_Legend_1958.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Crazy Water Crystals: &#39;The Legend of Texas Dehydrated Mineral Water&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1958-09-12</strong></td>\n<td>Retrospective radio tribute to 1930s border radio marketing pioneers.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Modern_Romances_Goodbye.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Modern Romances: &#39;Goodbye, Darling - A Story from Modern Romance Magazine&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1950-05-18</strong></td>\n<td>Emotional romantic drama adapted directly from the popular magazine.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n",
    "markdown": "# Archival Dispatch: 9 Master Broadcasts Dated Across Red Skelton, Blondie, Lucille Ball on Sports Newsreel, and Crazy Water Crystals\n\n**Date**: 2026-08-21  \n**Author**: radio index  \n**Tags**: Red Skelton, Clem Kadiddlehopper, Junior Mean Widdle Kid, Blondie, Dagwood Bumstead, Bill Stern, Lucille Ball, Jack Kramer, Crazy Water Crystals, Mineral Wells, Modern Romances, Original Filenames\n\n---\n\n## Batch 81 Forensic Discoveries\n\nBatch 81 recovers and dates 9 historical broadcasts spanning classic network comedy sketches, family sitcoms, early morning southwestern string band programs, celebrity sports interviews, and magazine dramatizations: 2 vintage 1948 broadcasts from Red Skelton on ***The Red Skelton Show*** (featuring Junior the Mean Widdle Kid and Clem Kadiddlehopper), Arthur Lake and Penny Singleton in ***Blondie*** (1944), Bill Stern interviewing Hollywood superstar Lucille Ball and tennis champion Jack Kramer on AFRS ***Sports Newsreel*** (1946–1947), 3 rare broadcasts from Mineral Wells, Texas sponsored by ***Crazy Water Crystals*** (1935–1958), and true confession drama on ***Modern Romances*** (1950).\n\n---\n\n## 1. *The Red Skelton Show* & *Blondie* (1944–1948)\n\nBeloved network comedy characters:\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Comedy Characters & Narrative |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Red_Skelton_Junior_Zoo.mp3` | **\"The Red Skelton Show: 'Junior the Mean Widdle Kid Goes to the Zoo'\"** | **1948-03-09** | Junior wreaks havoc among the exotic animals. |\n| `Red_Skelton_Clem_Department.mp3` | **\"The Red Skelton Show: 'Clem Kadiddlehopper at the Department Store'\"** | **1948-03-23** | Clem encounters revolving doors, escalators, and exasperated clerks. |\n| `Blondie_Missing_Package.mp3` | **\"Blondie: 'Dagwood's Missing Package & The Secret Formula'\"** | **1944-10-01** | Dagwood misplaces an important architectural blueprint package. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. *Bill Stern's Sports Newsreel*, *Crazy Water*, & *Modern Romances*\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Broadcast Substance |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Sports_Newsreel_Lucille_Ball.mp3` | **\"AFRS Sports Newsreel: Bill Stern interviews Lucille Ball\"** | **1946-09-27** | Lucille Ball discusses tennis, athletic conditioning, and Hollywood life. |\n| `Sports_Newsreel_Jack_Kramer.mp3` | **\"AFRS Sports Newsreel: Bill Stern interviews Jack Kramer & Bill Schroeder\"** | **1947-06-13** | US Tennis Champion Jack Kramer previewing international championship play. |\n| `Crazy_Water_Hotel_Prog_12.mp3` | **\"Crazy Water Crystals: 'Live from the Crazy Water Hotel' (Prog 12)\"** | **1935-08-14** | Early southwestern hillbilly string band music from Mineral Wells, Texas. |\n| `Crazy_Water_Hotel_Prog_17.mp3` | **\"Crazy Water Crystals: 'The Sunshine Special of Health and Happiness' (Prog 17)\"** | **1935-09-18** | High-energy fiddle tunes, gospel quartets, and country humor. |\n| `Crazy_Water_Legend_1958.mp3` | **\"Crazy Water Crystals: 'The Legend of Texas Dehydrated Mineral Water'\"** | **1958-09-12** | Retrospective radio tribute to 1930s border radio marketing pioneers. |\n| `Modern_Romances_Goodbye.mp3` | **\"Modern Romances: 'Goodbye, Darling - A Story from Modern Romance Magazine'\"** | **1950-05-18** | Emotional romantic drama adapted directly from the popular magazine. |\n"
