    "markdown": "# Archival Dispatch: 18 Master Broadcasts Dated Across Pennsylvania Keystone of Democracy, Backstage Wife, and The Son of Porthos\n\n**Date**: 2026-08-21  \n**Author**: radio index  \n**Tags**: Pennsylvania Keystone of Democracy, Valley Forge, Stephen Foster, Backstage Wife, Mary Noble, Frank Hummert, Anne Hummert, Claire Niesen, The Son of Porthos, Alexandre Dumas, Original Filenames\n\n---\n\n## Batch 66 Forensic Discoveries\n\nBatch 66 recovers and dates 18 classic radio broadcasts spanning educational historical docudramas, Golden Age daytime serial melodramas, and swashbuckling literary adventure serials: 6 founding episodes of the celebrated state historical series ***Pennsylvania: Keystone of Democracy*** (1941, produced by the Pennsylvania Historical Commission, covering George Washington at Valley Forge, the origins of the American steel industry, Stephen Foster, and the Pennsylvania long rifle), 6 consecutive serialized episodes of Frank and Anne Hummert's legendary NBC daytime soap opera ***Backstage Wife*** (May 1944, starring Claire Niesen as Mary Noble navigating the backstage murder of Oliver Wilson), and 6 serialized chapters of the 1939 syndicated adventure serial ***The Son of Porthos*** (adapting Alexandre Dumas' swashbuckling sequel to The Three Musketeers).\n\n---\n\n## 1. *Pennsylvania: Keystone of Democracy* — 1941 State Historical Series\n\nProduced by the Pennsylvania Historical and Museum Commission:\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Historical Commonwealth Heritage |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Penn_Keystone_Valley_Forge.mp3` | **\"Pennsylvania Keystone of Democracy: 'Washington at Valley Forge'\"** | **1941-10-14** | George Washington and the Continental Army endure the pivotal winter encampment. |\n| `Penn_Keystone_Steel_Industry.mp3` | **\"Pennsylvania Keystone of Democracy: 'Founding the Nation's Steel Industry'\"** | **1941-10-21** | Early iron forges and steel manufacture shaping the industrial revolution. |\n| `Penn_Keystone_Stephen_Foster.mp3` | **\"Pennsylvania Keystone of Democracy: 'Stephen Collins Foster & American Music'\"** | **1941-10-28** | Pittsburgh's legendary songwriter crafting timeless American folk melodies. |\n| `Penn_Keystone_Rifles_Wilderness.mp3` | **\"Pennsylvania Keystone of Democracy: 'Rifles in the Wilderness (Pennsylvania Rifle)'\"** | **1941-11-04** | Frontier craftsmanship of the legendary Pennsylvania long rifle. |\n| `Penn_Keystone_Women_Democracy.mp3` | **\"Pennsylvania Keystone of Democracy: 'Women for Democracy (Colonial Heroines)'\"** | **1941-11-11** | Revolutionary women fighting for liberty on the home front and battlefield. |\n| `Penn_Keystone_Dr_Reifsnyder.mp3` | **\"Pennsylvania Keystone of Democracy: 'Dr. Elizabeth Reifsnyder: Medical Pioneer'\"** | **1941-11-18** | Pioneering female physician establishing clinical hospitals in Shanghai. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. *Backstage Wife (Mary Noble)* — May 1944 NBC Murder Mystery Arc\n\nWritten by Frank & Anne Hummert, starring Claire Niesen as Mary Noble:\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Backstage Murder Mystery Arc |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Backstage_Wife_Murder_Wilson.mp3` | **\"Backstage Wife: 'The Murder of Oliver Wilson at Hamilton Theatre'\"** | **1944-05-08** | Panic backstage following the murder of a handsome young playboy. |\n| `Backstage_Wife_Larry_Jail.mp3` | **\"Backstage Wife: 'Larry Noble Awaits Murder Trial in City Jail'\"** | **1944-05-09** | Broadway matinee idol Larry Noble faces false homicide charges. |\n| `Backstage_Wife_Ramsey_Storms.mp3` | **\"Backstage Wife: 'Producer Harold Ramsey Storms Larry's Dressing Room'\"** | **1944-05-10** | Tempers flare as theatrical producers scramble to save the production. |\n| `Backstage_Wife_Rupert_Barlow.mp3` | **\"Backstage Wife: 'Mary Confronts Backer Rupert Barlow'\"** | **1944-05-11** | Mary fights to reclaim securities given to a sinister financial backer. |\n| `Backstage_Wife_Long_Island_Drive.mp3` | **\"Backstage Wife: 'The Drive from Long Island & The Stranger'\"** | **1944-05-12** | A late-night drive into Manhattan reveals unexpected tailing vehicles. |\n| `Backstage_Wife_Victor_Calls.mp3` | **\"Backstage Wife: 'Victor the Chauffeur Calls the Hotel Room'\"** | **1944-05-15** | A mysterious phone call from an ex-chauffeur offers vital murder clues. |\n\n---\n\n## 3. *The Son of Porthos* — 1939 Alexandre Dumas Adventure Serial\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Swashbuckling Chapter Arc |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Son_Porthos_Fall_Pryborne.mp3` | **\"The Son of Porthos: 'The Fall of Pryborne & The Castle Siege'\"** | **1939-07-03** | The siege of Pryborne Castle and a daring escape through secret passages. |\n| `Son_Porthos_Kings_Commission.mp3` | **\"The Son of Porthos: 'The King's Commission at St. Cybert'\"** | **1939-07-10** | Receiving secret royal orders from the court of King Louis. |\n| `Son_Porthos_Fortune_Teller.mp3` | **\"The Son of Porthos: 'The Fortune Teller's House on Rue du Bois'\"** | **1939-07-17** | Uncovering a cryptic prophecy in the Paris underworld. |\n| `Son_Porthos_Secret_Passage.mp3` | **\"The Son of Porthos: 'The Secret Passage from the Manor'\"** | **1939-07-24** | Infiltrating the fortress through subterranean waterway tunnels. |\n| `Son_Porthos_Court_Louis.mp3` | **\"The Son of Porthos: 'The Court of King Louis & The Royal Musketeers'\"** | **1939-07-31** | Royal court intrigue and musketeer swordplay in Paris. |\n| `Son_Porthos_City_Gates_Duel.mp3` | **\"The Son of Porthos: 'Duel at the City Gates'\"** | **1939-08-07** | A climactic dawn duel to defend the honour of the realm. |\n"
