    "markdown": "# Archival Dispatch: 15 Historical Broadcasts Dated Across Armed Forces Command Performance and Strange As It Seems\n\n**Date**: 2026-08-21  \n**Author**: radio index  \n**Tags**: Command Performance, AFRS, Bing Crosby, Ethel Merman, Strange As It Seems, John Hix, Original Filenames\n\n---\n\n## Batch 15 Forensic Discoveries\n\nBatch 15 resolves 15 historic network and syndicated broadcasts: 5 flagship wartime and postwar episodes of Armed Forces Radio Service's ***Command Performance*** (starring Bing Crosby, Ethel Merman, Jackie Gleason, Benny Goodman, and Lionel Barrymore) and 10 weekly episodes from John Hix's famous 1939 syndicated docudrama series ***Strange As It Seems*** (sponsored by Ex-Lax).\n\n---\n\n## 1. *Command Performance* — AFRS Master Disc Broadcasts Dated\n\nProduced by the War Department and Armed Forces Radio Service for American troops worldwide:\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | All-Star Cast & Repertoire |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Command_Performance_145_Merman_Lewis.mp3` | **\"Command Performance 145: Ethel Merman, Joe E. Lewis, Connie Boswell\"** | **1944-11-01** | Broadway legend Ethel Merman and comedian Joe E. Lewis headline for overseas GIs. |\n| `Command_Performance_152_Goodman_Romay.mp3` | **\"Command Performance 152: Benny Goodman, Lina Romay, Hoagy Carmichael\"** | **1944-12-16** | King of Swing Benny Goodman sextet with singer Lina Romay and Hoagy Carmichael. |\n| `Command_Performance_198_Crosby_Maxwell.mp3` | **\"Command Performance 198: Bing Crosby, Marilyn Maxwell, Lionel Barrymore\"** | **1945-10-28** | Postwar victory broadcast with Bing Crosby, Marilyn Maxwell, and Lionel Barrymore. |\n| `Command_Performance_392_Whiting_Niles.mp3` | **\"Command Performance 392: Margaret Whiting, Wendell Niles, Jack Smith, Steve Allen\"** | **1949-07-24** | AFRS summer variety showcase featuring young Steve Allen and Margaret Whiting. |\n| `Command_Performance_479_Gray_Gleason.mp3` | **\"Command Performance 479: Coleen Gray, Jackie Gleason, Fred Allen\"** | **1950-02-12** | Comedy sketch showcase featuring Jackie Gleason and radio giant Fred Allen. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. *Strange As It Seems* — John Hix 1939 Syndication Discs Dated\n\nAdapted from John Hix's syndicated newspaper cartoon feature, exploring historical oddities:\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Historical Enigma |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Strange_As_It_Seems_The_Diamond_Dinner.mp3` | **\"The Diamond Dinner (Maan, Michigan Mystery)\"** | **1939-09-14** | Mysterious garden discovery in Maan, Michigan. |\n| `Strange_As_It_Seems_The_Statue_Of_Irony.mp3` | **\"The Statue of Irony\"** | **1939-09-21** | The dramatic origins of monument sculptures. |\n| `Strange_As_It_Seems_For_Whom_Was_PA_Named.mp3` | **\"For Whom Was Pennsylvania Named\"** | **1939-09-28** | The colonial history and namesake of William Penn's father. |\n| `Strange_As_It_Seems_The_Raw_Deal.mp3` | **\"The Raw Deal: Albrecht von Wallenstein\"** | **1939-10-05** | The tragic fate of the Bohemian military commander. |\n| `Strange_As_It_Seems_Fort_Blunder.mp3` | **\"Fort Blunder at Lake Champlain\"** | **1939-10-12** | Post-War of 1812 US fort built on Canadian territory by mistake. |\n| `Strange_As_It_Seems_Wreck_Of_The_Hesperus.mp3` | **\"The Wreck of the Hesperus Mystery\"** | **1939-10-19** | Nautical facts behind Longfellow's famous reef of Norman's Woe ballad. |\n| `Strange_As_It_Seems_The_Neck_Verse.mp3` | **\"The Neck Verse: Benefit of Clergy\"** | **1939-10-26** | Ancient English legal loophole of reading Psalm 51 to escape the gallows. |\n| `Strange_As_It_Seems_Man_Fate_Could_Not_Conquer.mp3` | **\"The Man Fate Could Not Conquer\"** | **1939-11-02** | Incredible endurance feats across historical disasters. |\n| `Strange_As_It_Seems_Cure_For_Rabies.mp3` | **\"The Old Fashioned Cure for Rabies\"** | **1939-11-09** | 19th-century medical folklore before Louis Pasteur's vaccine. |\n| `Strange_As_It_Seems_The_Martyr_To_Etiquette.mp3` | **\"The Martyr to Etiquette\"** | **1939-11-16** | Royal European court rituals that caused historical disasters. |\n"
